Z||000016||Formula88||08-09-2001||12:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JBGehling:<BR><B>I guess the big  white circle by the back wheel-well is the flash? <BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>It's call a "lens flare."  It's from light, either natural or from the flash, that's reflecting off the lens of the camera itself.  Some filters are designed to purposely create this effect, but you generally try to avoid it.  You can usually get around it just by changing your light angle slightly.<BR>||||reg||1
